cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "pupil-ieeg-matlab: analysis code for pupil-linked human intracranial high-gamma coupling"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB analysis code for relating spontaneous high-gamma activity to pupil
  diameter in human intracranial recordings. The primary analysis is a linear
  mixed model of a continuous signed coupling amplitude, applied to every
  contact with no thresholding or selection, with contacts nested in electrode
  shafts nested in patients and FDR-controlled region families. Also implements
  the spatial-gradient, frequency-profile and neuromodulator-density analyses,
  a variogram-matched spatial null, and the earlier dichotomised hurdle model
  retained as a secondary comparison. Code and methods only; no participant
  data.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nielspac177/pupil-ieeg-matlab-public"
keywords:
  - pupillometry
  - intracranial EEG
  - high-gamma
  - arousal
  - hippocampus
  - mixed-effects models
  - reproducibility
authors:
